    "historical_decision": "Siam and Thailand are official-name phases of one Thai state identity. The government changed the country name to Thailand in 1939, restored Siam in September 1945, and Siam notified the United Nations on 11 May 1949 that it had changed its name to Thailand. The name changes do not constitute state extinction/replacement.",
    "first_siam_designation_boundary_note": "The first Siam designation begins in 1851 only as the earliest currently modeled ATLAS Activity that explicitly uses the Siam name; this is a coverage floor, not a claim that Siam was first adopted in 1851. The 1939 end is kept at year granularity/approximate because reviewed sources distinguish the June policy announcement from later legislative/royal-assent steps.",
    "second_siam_designation_boundary_note": "U.S. diplomatic records state that Thailand/Thais were discarded as of 7 September 1945 and replaced by Siam/Siamese. The United Nations records the subsequent change from Siam to Thailand on 11 May 1949."
  },
